A1. Even though this is yellow it's apt to hit you in the eye. ~ LEMON
A4. This gets many a good second-hand car owner out of a hole. ~ NAG
A6. What Jesse James dealt in. ~ THEFT
A9. What got after Jesse James. ~ POSE
A11. Not well done. ~ RARE
A13. Collectors. ~ PESTS
A14. What pedestrians have to be to get by. ~ ALERT
A16. What amateur golfers have trouble getting away from. ~ TEE
A18. What all peaches should be. ~ EATABLE
A20. An animal that acts like a man. ~ ASS
A22. What seamen take along when they go down to the sea in ships. ~ YAWL
A24. The hair apparent. ~ GRAY
A25. It costs a lot to get this in the Stock Exchange. ~ SEAT
A26. Never found in "dead ones." ~ PEP
A28. This is very woolly. ~ YARN
A29. Found in the yard. ~ FEET
A30. Some of these are ramblers. ~ ROSES
A32. These are impregnated with alkaline soap. ~ LYES
A34. Found next to the homebrew in the best cellars. ~ COAL
A35. This is always at your finger's tip. ~ NAIL
A36. What kind of people have the best cellars? ~ RICH
A39. Billy's lady friend. ~ NANNY
A41. A piece of cheese is much better this way. ~ AGED
A44. What Mr. Wrigley would have everybody choose to do. ~ CHEW
A45. This is always running from the sun. ~ RAY
A46. An adjective meaning single; sole. ~ ONLY
A47. He who fights and runs away, lives to do this another day. ~ READ
A50. Having toes. ~ TOED
A52. Unnecessary activity, or bustle. ~ ADO
A53. What the barber who shaves you talks about. ~ MASSAGE
A57. What poets have difficulty paying the rent with. ~ ODE
A58. Tex Rickard's chief interest. (Believe this and we'll tell you another.) ~ SPORT
A60. Bossy's gift to humanity. (This is kine o' nice.) ~ CREAM
A62. Join this and see the next world. ~ ARMY
A63. To depend on with confidence. ~ RELY
A64. What do Romeos do for their Juliets. ~ YEARN
A65. A feminine pronoun. ~ SHE
A66. How do married men look. ~ SEEDY

D1. What kind of a person is an aviator? ~ LOFTY
D2. This is open to poets. ~ OPE
D3. What do you follow wherever you go? ~ NOSE
D4. Where the wise bird spends his evenings. ~ NEST
D5. This is the clutch. ~ GRAB
D6. Where peaches come from. ~ TREE
D7. A feminine pronoun. ~ HER
D8. What the moon makes some people. ~ TIPSY
D10. A shining light on Broadway. ~ STAR
D12. A verb meaning "to join." ~ ALLY
D13. A small olive-green fly-catcher. ~ PEWEE
D15. To linger. ~ TARRY
D17. Freedom from pain. ~ EASE
D19. These sprang from old family trees. ~ APES
D21. Those who never get crazy about anything. ~ SANE
D23. How we find the door to success. ~ LATCHED
D24. A gentleman of the old school. ~ GALLANT
D26. A cold region. ~ POLAR
D27. This is hardly worth a cent any more. ~ PENNY
D29. Something to wrap baby in. ~ FUR
D30. What Nurmi did on the road to fame. ~ RAN
D31. To utter in words. ~ SAY
D33. How papa feels after the holidays. ~ SAD
D37. How the cake looks sweeter. ~ ICED
D38. Confusion. ~ CHAOS
D40. Family jars. ~ NAGS
D42. What vertical 40 causes. ~ GLOOM
D43. How the pretty flapper finds herself. ~ EYED
D47. Days when the sun never shines. ~ RAINY
D48. What careless pedestrians come to. ~ HARM
D49. A monster of our childhood dreams. ~ OGRE
D51. This leads many a bird into trouble. ~ DECOY
D53. This follows every wild night. ~ MORN
D54. Pens. ~ STYS
D55. A lot of square rods. ~ ACRE
D56. Slippery fish. ~ EELS
D59. Equality in value. ~ PAR
D61. What "yes men" say. ~ AYE


